              "type": "text",
              "text": "A fair six-sided die is rolled six times. What is the probability that each of the rolls resulted in a different number?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{5}{324}$.\n\nMultiply the successive probabilities of rolling a number that has not appeared previously.",
      "worked": "The first roll can be any number. Each subsequent roll must avoid all numbers already recorded.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{all different})&=\\frac{6}{6}\\times\\frac{5}{6}\\times\\frac{4}{6}\\times\\frac{3}{6}\\times\\frac{2}{6}\\times\\frac{1}{6}\\\\P(\\text{all different})&=\\frac{720}{46656}\\\\P(\\text{all different})&=\\frac{5}{324}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 46
  },
